{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And a mist</b> — like \"smoke,\" and like it \"a day of cloud\" (Lam. 2:2), for a day of calamity is called a day of cloud and fog. The meaning is that a mist rose from the earth by the force of the luminaries and watered the ground and brought forth vegetation. The Gaon [Saadia] said that its meaning is: and no mist would rise from the earth."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The Hebrew citation דב\"ר לב לה appears to refer to Lamentations (איכה, Eikhah) 2:2, where יום אידם occurs; the abbreviation resolution is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:46.117915829Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}